      "name": null,
      "problem": "$(-1+7.35)^{0}\\times {5}^{-3}=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, we compute the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n(-1+7.35)^{0}\\times {5}^{-3}=(6.35)^{0}\\times {5}^{-3}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that $(6.35)^{0}=1.$ So, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6.35)^{0}\\times {5}^{-3} & = \\\\ 1\\times {5}^{-3} & = \\\\ {5}^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{5}^{-3}=\\frac{1}{{5}^{3}}=\\frac{1}{125}.\n$$",
